Directory "no-such-dir" does not exist.

Usage:
    ingest-music [options] <downloadDir> <ingestDir> [opusCopyDir]

    downloadDir   directory holding the freshly downloaded music to ingest
    ingestDir     directory the cleaned/encoded library is written to
                  (created if it does not exist)
    opusCopyDir   directory the 120 kbps Opus copies are written to
                  (optional; defaults to the sibling folder "<ingestDir>opus")

Options:
    -h, --help    Print this help page.
    -c, --beets-config <file>
                  The beets config the tagging phase runs with. The one that
                  ships with the package is the default, and its
                  "directory: ." resolves to <ingestDir> because beets runs
                  from inside it - a config that names a directory of its own
                  moves the library there.
                  Default the shipped medialib/config/beets.yaml
    -j, --jobs <jobs>
                  Run up to <jobs> encoder processes in parallel
                  (default: the number of CPU cores).
    -k, --keep [part]
                  keep <part>: takes nothing away. The one part is resolution:
                  the source's bit depth and sample rate, which a run otherwise
                  turns into 16-bit at 48 kHz or less. Kept, the lossless copy
                  stays at the source's resolution; the Opus copies are not
                  affected. A bare -k keeps every part, which today is this
                  one. A folder literally named "resolution" is written
                  ./resolution: the word after -k is the part when it is one.
    -o, --offline Offline: the tagging phase is skipped, so the run reaches no
                  network and needs no beets.
                  Default false
    -v, --verbose Also say why each item was handled the way it was, and on a
                  failure print the tool's whole output rather than its last
                  lines.
    -q, --quiet   Print errors only - no progress and no warnings.
    -x, --set <name=value>
                  Override a setting for this run: name=value, repeatable. The
                  value is held where the environment holds it, so it wins over
                  the settings file; a secret is refused - the settings file is
                  where it goes. The settings page lists the names.

Dependencies:
    ffmpeg, mkvtoolnix, ImageMagick, rsync, fdupes, beets (unless -o), and the
    mutagen package for this Python (chapter embedding). Optional: flock
    (numbers the progress lines). Also invokes the sibling commands
    convert-audio, clean-folder-structure and cue-to-chapters.
